  "entity_raw": {
    "name_raw": "Flexible Wizardry",
    "definition_type_raw": null,
    "source_book_raw": "Advanced Class Guide pg. 148",
    "definition_raw": "Source Advanced Class Guide pg. 148\nYou have learned a trick that makes your spellcasting more flexible.\n\nPrerequisites: Spell Mastery, wizard level 1st.\n\nBenefit: When you prepare your spells each day, you can choose to keep a number of spell slots equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) flexibly prepared. Instead of preparing a single spell within each of these slots, you can partially prepare two spells. Anytime after you prepare these flexible slots, you can spend a full-round action to finalize one slot, choosing one of the two spells to be finished and fully prepared in that slot.",
